// design.md §15 Semver lock (6563): a C-like enum without #[repr] has
// compiler-chosen discriminants; a caller using .discriminant() on it relies
// on a local property, not a semver contract, and `karac explain` on such a
// call says so.
enum Plain { A, B }
fn code() -> u32 { Plain.B.discriminant() }
fn main() { println(f"{code()}"); }
